## Test findings and Red reasons

- A3-1/C3-1 (preview.sh:75-93), 2 tests:
  - "A3-1 keeps an existing preview folder byte-identical after an input
    check refusal" — fails because the refused run overlays the existing
    preview folder (index.html changes, docs copy stays).
  - "A3-1 leaves no new parent folder after a refusal into a new nested
    preview folder" — fails because the created parent
    `.tmp/a3-1-nested-parent` stays after the leaf is removed.
- A3-2/C3-3 (real-work.ts:178-185), 8 tests (4 per file):
  - null `coverage.runs` → current line is `input-check: run-sum`; the
    contract pins `input-check: schema`.
  - number in `first_run_date`, string in `share_known_route`, missing
    `generated_on` → tool exits 0 (input-check file) or the preview pipeline
    exits 1 with a Python traceback; the contract pins exit 2 with
    `input-check: schema`, no traceback, no half-built preview folder.
- A3-3 (preview.sh:80-87), 1 test: a planted dangling symlink
  `<preview>/real-work.json -> <repo>/docs/real-work.json` makes the second
  preview exit 0 and create `docs/real-work.json` through the link; the
  contract pins exit 2, no docs write, one refusal line on stdout.
- C3-2/A3-4 (preview.sh:107-113 and :136), 1 test: a second preview over a
  published `docs/index.html` doubles the nav links (2 instead of 1 of
  each).
- B2-1 (publish.ts:92, :136; preview.sh:107 sha256_file), 3 tests:
  - dangling symlink under docs during publish → exit 1 with a statSync
    stack; contract pins exit 2 with `publish: drift dangling.txt`, no stack.
  - unreadable file under docs (mode 000, present at preview time) during
    publish → exit 1 with a sha256File stack; contract pins exit 2 with
    `publish: drift locked.txt`, no stack.
  - dangling entry under docs during preview.sh → exit 1 with a Python
    traceback in `sha256_file`; contract pins exit 2, no traceback.

