```

All 15 new tests fail on the missing behavior (not on syntax or setup).
All 76 existing tests still pass.

## Notes for the Green role

- The null-`coverage.runs` case must refuse with `input-check: schema`, so
  the type check must run before the run-sum check.
- The A3-1 nested case expects the whole created chain to go
  (`.tmp` absent after the refusal in a fresh repo). Both suggested fixes
  satisfy it.
- A3-2 in the preview-gate file pins the pipeline property too: exit 2, no
  half-built preview folder, no traceback.
- Vitest gotcha: do not interpolate raw child stderr into an expect
  message when the child crashes with a stack; vitest's source-map parser
  aborts the worker. The new tests use static status messages.

## Spec gap (default applied)

- A3-3 refusal line: `spec.md` names no refusal line format for a symlink
  planted inside an existing preview folder. Default applied: assert exit 2,
  no docs write, and exactly one non-empty refusal line on stdout, without
  pinning its text. The Green role may reuse `preview: refused path <value>`
  or any single-line refusal; it should document the chosen line in the
  preview.sh header.

